.TH QUADRF-RF-VISION 1 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-rf-vision \- spatial RF phase scatter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-rf-vision
.RB [ \-\-headless ]
.RB [ \-\-camera ]
.RB [ \-\-cam_w
.IR W ]
.RB [ \-\-cam_h
.IR H ]
.RB [ \-\-cam_fps
.IR fps ]
.RB [ \-\-cam_cmd
.IR command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sweeps the local oscillator, reads the four CSI channels, and plots the phase
gradient of each bin as a point whose position is the direction it arrived
from. Strong, stable emitters settle into tight clusters; noise spreads out.
.PP
The scatter is drawn in an SDL window and also served over a WebSocket on port
8000, which is what the browser AR page at
.I /AR/
consumes. Overlay settings saved from that page are kept in
.IR /var/lib/quadrf/demos/ar_settings.json .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Do not open the SDL window; serve the WebSocket feed only.
.TP
.B \-\-camera
Underlay the scatter with a live camera image captured through libcamera-vid.
.TP
.BI \-\-cam_w " W" ", " \-\-cam_h " H"
Camera capture resolution. Default: 640x480.
.TP
.BI \-\-cam_fps " fps"
Camera frame rate. Default: 30.
.TP
.BI \-\-cam_cmd " command"
Replace the capture command. It must write raw I420 frames on standard output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/quadrf/demos/ar_settings.json
Overlay settings shared with the AR page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf-psd (1),
.BR quadrf-jtag (1)
